WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.120
♪ Codex! ♪

00:06.160 --> 00:08.220
When you were a kid, did you dream

00:08.220 --> 00:10.660
of building video games
for your favorite console?

00:10.910 --> 00:12.570
Well, hold on to your Power Glove,

00:12.580 --> 00:15.830
because with the ModRetro Chromatic plugin
for ChatGPT,

00:15.850 --> 00:19.120
you can use Codex to build and play
real Game Boy Color games

00:19.120 --> 00:21.040
the way they were meant to be played,

00:21.040 --> 00:24.820
on a tiny 2.5-inch screen
that fits in the palm of your hand.

00:24.920 --> 00:27.540
Oh, and importantly, small enough
to hide in your lunchbox

00:27.540 --> 00:29.040
when the teacher is looking.

00:30.350 --> 00:31.780
[ruler smacks]

00:31.990 --> 00:34.020
Ah! Seems unnecessary.

00:34.870 --> 00:35.960
Jeez.

00:36.260 --> 00:38.060
Anyway, uh, here's how you get started.

00:38.260 --> 00:41.180
Download the plugin from the marketplace
in the ChatGPT app.

00:41.380 --> 00:43.780
The plugin is set up to help you
develop games locally

00:43.780 --> 00:46.820
with open source tools
like GBDK and GB Studio.

00:47.433 --> 00:49.723
Ask Codex to use the ModRetro plugin

00:49.723 --> 00:51.563
to build any game you can imagine.

00:52.033 --> 00:54.463
The plugin also has tools to generate
the pixel art,

00:54.473 --> 00:57.453
tile maps, and audio
that you'll need for a real game.

00:57.753 --> 00:59.433
When you create a game with the plugin,

00:59.433 --> 01:02.073
you also get a fully functional
GB Studio project,

01:02.073 --> 01:05.453
which you can use along with Codex
to build and tweak your game.

01:05.713 --> 01:07.353
The plugin ships with a preview window

01:07.353 --> 01:10.013
you can use to quickly iterate
on the game in the browser.

01:10.193 --> 01:12.473
And using annotations in ChatGPT,

01:12.473 --> 01:16.193
the plugin allows you to annotate specific
parts of the game to request changes.

01:16.943 --> 01:19.073
When your game's ready
to test on a device,

01:19.083 --> 01:22.183
connect a Chromatic via USB,
select your device,

01:22.253 --> 01:24.973
and flash your game to memory
on the current game cartridge.

01:25.093 --> 01:27.153
Be careful, though. Whatever ROM
was previously

01:27.153 --> 01:29.533
on the cartridge is permanently deleted.

01:29.563 --> 01:31.453
And I don't want you losing
that rare monster

01:31.453 --> 01:33.800
you got at the Toys R Us event
when you were nine years old.

01:34.600 --> 01:35.783
You don’t have to wait for a device

01:35.783 --> 01:37.153
to start creating your game.

01:37.193 --> 01:39.753
The ModRetro Chromatic plugin is available

01:39.753 --> 01:41.893
in the ChatGPT desktop app right now.

01:41.973 --> 01:44.323
And trust me, this is gonna be really fun.

01:45.153 --> 01:47.323
Oh, hey, uh, do you mind if I get
next on that?

01:47.563 --> 01:48.203
No?

01:48.373 --> 01:49.943
Like, poss...
